{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:UGB.BuchbergerPBW.buchberger_theorem","@type":"LeanModule","name":"UGB.BuchbergerPBW.buchberger_theorem","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Basic"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.BuchbergerPBW.buchberger_theorem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.BuchbergerPBW.buchberger_theorem","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/BuchbergerPBW/buchberger_theorem.lean#L48-L77","doc":"**Buchberger's criterion.**\n\n`sys` is a Gröbner–Shirshov basis **iff** every overlap S-polynomial\nand every inclusion S-polynomial of `sys` reduces to the zero\nelement. This is the manuscript's iff \"GS basis ⟺ all S-polynomials\nhave zero remainder\", expressed on the concrete S-polynomial\nstructures `OverlapComposition` / `InclusionComposition`.\n\nThe statement is a **concrete biconditional** between\n`IsGrobnerShirshovBasis` and a conjunction of two `∀`-resolution\nclauses — substantive content the former `holds : Prop` lacked.\nProved by unfolding the GS-basis structure. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:thm:ugb-buchberger","label":"thm:ugb-buchberger","md":"unital-groebner-bases/buchberger-and-pbw/buchberger-theorem.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}